            <div xml:id="d731">

                <pb facs="0650" n="641" sameAs="frus:frus1940v02/pg641"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">740.0011 European War 1939/5334: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Consul at Leopoldville</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Mallon</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic"
                        >to the Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Leopoldville</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1940-08-30T12:00:00+01:00">August 30,
                            1940—noon</date>.<lb/>[Received August 30—10:40 a.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>Referring to my telegram of August 28 De Larminat appointed High Commissioner of
                    France Libre for French Equatorial Africa and Cameroon. <hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Coup d’état</hi> effected without bloodshed. Husson roughly handled but
                    unhurt, expects to leave Leopoldville for Dakar as soon as possible. Should I
                    call officially on De Larminat?</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Mallon</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
